rry_parcel","ring_doorbell","hand_parcel"]},"scenes":{"road":["road"],"town":["road"],"village":["road"],"depot":["road","hub"]},"notes":"One atlas per page.  \"road\" (gbPages.resident) stays resident wherever a 금방 courier or crew member can be seen: carry_parcel, ring_doorbell, hand_parcel, the cap on every head frame and the jacket / vest in idle / walk / talk / wave / happy.  \"hub\" holds scan, sort_parcel and tape_box: load it while the depot (금방 물류센터) is revealed and drop it afterwards.  It also holds the road-anim frames of the depot crew's own v4 garments (texture memory): top_sweater (the packer) and top_parka (picker, dockhand) in carry_parcel / ring_doorbell / hand_parcel; a courier (jacket, cap, scarf) never needs it.  Ask pageNeeded(person, anim) (per person) inside the sprite's has() predicate: a depot-crew road anim without \"hub\" falls back (carry_parcel -> walk, ring_doorbell / hand_parcel -> talk / idle); the docks are part of the depot scene, so the dockhand's carry_parcel there has it."},"crew":{"gb_driver":{"label":{"ko":"금방 기사님 (쌩쌩이 · 부릉이 · 씽씽이)","en":"Geumbang driver"},"names":["쌩쌩이","부릉이","씽씽이"],"signature":["carry_parcel","ring_doorbell","hand_parcel"]},"gb_picker":{"label":{"ko":"금방 피커 (쏙쏙이)","en":"Geumbang picker"},"names":["쏙쏙이"],"signature":["sort_parcel","carry_parcel","wave"]},"gb_packer":{"label":{"ko":"금방 포장 담당 (척척이)","en":"Geumbang packer"},"names":["척척이"],"signature":["tape_box","scan","happy"]},"gb_sorter":{"label":{"ko":"금방 상하차 담당 (영차)","en":"Geumbang dockhand"},"names":["영차"],"signature":["carry_parcel","scan","sort_parcel"]},"gb_dispatcher":{"label":{"ko":"방금순 팀장 (배차 담당)","en":"Team lead Bang Geumsun (dispatcher)"},"names":["방금순 팀장"],"signature":["scan","talk","hand_parcel"]},"gb_rider":{"label":{"ko":"금방 개썰매 기사 (뽀득이)","en":"Geumbang sled rider"},"names":["뽀득이"],"signature":["carry_parcel","ring_doorbell","hand_parcel"]},"gb_night":{"label":{"ko":"금방 밤 기사님 (반짝이 · 살금이)","en":"Geumbang night driver"},"names":["반짝이","살금이"],"signature":["carry_parcel","hand_parcel","idle"]}},"brand":{"gold":"#F2B33D","goldDark":"#D9962A","cream":"#F4EDE0","charcoal":"#3B3F52","navy":"#2B4F7E","mark":"금방이 (gold disc + goldDark rim + cream sticker border, a face-on cream parcel with navy dot eyes, pink cheeks, an \"o\" mouth and a cream sparkle above; symmetric, no letters)","markSource":"gb_mark_thumbs.mark(A)","notes":"Tinted: only the jacket body (top: gold, goldDark for the night crew).  Fixed colour (untinted, one layer each - preset colours for these slots do nothing): the jacket trim / cuffs / marks (cream + the mark), the whole vest (gold, goldDark hem, cream stripes, the mark), the whole cap (charcoal crown, navy ear flaps, gold band / brim / button, the mark) and every held item (the parcel: deep kraft with a pale lid, gold tape cross, cream label, the mark sticker)."},"hub":{"workHeightsM":{"counterTop":0.3,"parcelOnCounter":0.2,"boxTop":0.42,"shelf":{"NE":0.86,"SE":0.62,"E":0.64},"tote":0.34},"rule":"Stand the worker at staffPoint + offsetPx (screen px; depth = that point).  liftPx = frontTopPx - parcelBottomPx + 2 (rounded up; 0 where places[].liftPx says so): draw the clerk / packer liftPx higher (sprite y - liftPx, depth unchanged), standing on a hidden step behind the counter / table, so the parcel the game draws at bases.boxPoint.scan / .tape_box (bottom = [bx, by]) stands 2 px behind the front edge of the real counter / table top, under the scanner beam / the tape roller.  Keep the lift for every anim played there (scan, talk, idle, tape_box ...).  Pickers (racks) and the dockhand need no lift.  The box (tape_box) and the parcel on the counter (scan) are gb_parcel_m at 0.20 m (scale it so topPx = 0.20 x 55.4 px).  places[staffN].anim = what to play there (staff1 at the conveyor: sort_parcel, no lift).","places":{"staff0":{"role":"clerk","point":[-260,-60],"dir":"SW","anim":"scan","offsetPx":[24,12],"frontTopPx":45,"frontTopRangePx":[41,48],"parcelBottomPx":8.0,"liftPx":39,"why":"방금순 slides 27 px along the counter: the counter's yellow display board no longer covers her face and glasses (critique M2)"},"staff1":{"role":"packer","point":[7,-21],"dir":"SW","anim":"sort_parcel","offsetPx":[0,0],"frontTopPx":34,"frontTopRangePx":[31,37],"parcelBottomPx":6.1,"liftPx":12,"why":"at the conveyor the packer picks parcels off the belt (sort_parcel on a 12 px step): the belt hides his boots, the mittens and the parcel show over it; tape_box needed a 30 px step that put his boots on the far rail (critique M3)"},"staff2":{"role":"packer","point":[171,55],"dir":"SW","anim":"tape_box","offsetPx":[-20,-10],"frontTopPx":31,"frontTopRangePx":[28,34],"parcelBottomPx":6.1,"liftPx":27,"why":"the middle of the packing table, left of the bubble-wrap roll: the roll no longer covers his mittens, the tape gun and the box (critique M3)"}}},"parcelDepth":{"carry_parcel":{"S":0.0045,"SE":0.0045,"E":0.0045,"NE":-0.0001,"N":-0.0001},"ring_doorbell":{"E":0.0045,"NE":0.0045,"N":0.0045},"hand_parcel":{"SE":0.0045,"E":0.0045,"NE":0.0045}},"items":{"carry_parcel":"held_parcel_gb (main): the medium 금방 parcel hugged at the belly.  With {noItems:true} the game draws its own gb_parcel_s/m/l (assets/geumbang) at bases[b].boxPoint.carry_parcel[dir][i] = [cx, cy, bx, by] (centre and bottom-centre, px from the anchor; mirrored dirs negate x) at parcelDepth.carry_parcel (+0.0045 in S / SE / E, -0.0001 in NE / N).  Move at bases[b].groundSpeed.carry_parcel[dir] px/s, or play at timeScale = clamp(speed / groundSpeed, 0.8, 1.8) so the feet do not skate.","ring_doorbell":"held_parcel_gb (main).  Doors face the camera, so the bell is rung facing NE / NW (or N): there the parcel rides under the RIGHT arm on the camera side (turned, short side against the body; that arm, mitten and the parcel are drawn over the coat: timeline zfront) and the LEFT mitten presses the bell; facing E / W it is tucked under the left arm in front of the belly and the right mitten presses.  {noItems}: gb_parcel_m at boxPoint.ring_doorbell at parcelDepth.ring_doorbell (+0.0045 in every dir: over the coat).  bellPoint.ring_doorbell[dir][i] = the pressing mitten tip (impactFrame 2 = 띵, 3 = 동) -> sfx_gb_doorbell + fx_gb_bell there.  Facing away (NE / NW / N) that mitten and the bell are behind the head: draw the flash behind the doll (depth -0.0001; the head hides most of it, the 띵-동 sound carries the beat), never over the face.  Plays once and holds the last frame (waiting at the door), then onDone.","hand_parcel":"no item is drawn: fly the real gb_parcel_* from handPoint.hand_parcel[dir][i] (between the palms; facing away (NE / NW) at the camera-side mitten pushed out to the side, where the parcel stays visible) at parcelDepth.hand_parcel (+0.0045: over the coat); draw it there on frames 0-2, it leaves on frame 3, frame 5 = the little bow; plays once, holds the bow, then onDone (-> wave).","scan":"held_scanner (right fist); beamPoint.scan[dir][i] = [wx, wy, tx, ty]: the scanner window and the beam target (the parcel top on the counter).  impactFrame 2 = 삑 (sfx_gb_scan + a short beam / glint from window to target).  The game draws the parcel lying on the counter (gb_parcel_m, 0.20 m: scale = 0.20 x 55.4 / topPx) with its bottom-centre at bases.boxPoint.scan[dir][i] = [cx, cy, bx, by] (top = the beam target) at the clerk's depth + 0.005 (over the body, under the head / arms / scanner).  The clerk works behind the counter: lift per hub.places.","sort_parcel":"held_parcel_gb (small) between the mittens on frames 1-4 (taken from the shelf on 1, dropped into the tote on 4: the rack stack drops one step at frame 1); handPoint.sort_parcel[dir][i] = between the mittens.  Shelf height per dir (NE reaches up, SE / E chest high): hub.workHeightsM.shelf.","tape_box":"held_tapegun (right fist), the left mitten holds the flaps; the game draws the box (gb_parcel_m at 0.20 m: scale = 0.20 x 55.4 / topPx) with its bottom-centre at bases.boxPoint.tape_box[dir][i] = [cx, cy, bx, by] (still; top centre = cx, cy) at the packer's depth + 0.005 (over the body, under the head / arms / tape gun); tapePoint.tape_box[dir][i] = the roller running along the box top.  impactFrame 3 = 찌익 + the cutting flick (sfx_gb_tape).  Lift per hub.places.","gbOthers":"noItems skips every anim item (animItems); the parcel / scanner / tape gun frames are drawn automatically otherwise."},"merge":["Merge order: assets/townfolk \"townfolk\" <- (assets/townfolk2) <- (assets/beachfolk) <- (assets/cityfolk) <- (assets/officefolk) <- assets/geumbangfolk \"geumbangfolk\".  The fragment REQUIRES only townfolk: it merges whether or not townfolk2 / beachfolk / cityfolk / officefolk are loaded (v4.3 loads townfolk + officefolk + geumbangfolk; no cityfolk).  tools/geumbangfolk_compose.js mergeGeumbangfolk(man, ...fragments, manGb) = cityfolk_compose.mergeTownfolkFragments + the post rule below.","Generic merge (cityfolk.merge): atlases concatenate; anims, timeline, headPoses, parts, z, tintRef, palettes, frameAtlas add NEW keys only (a redefinition is an error); frameAtlasExt routes the geumbangfolk frames of layers an earlier fragment owns (limbs, top_parka, top_sweater, bot_pants, shoe_boots, acc_scarf in the crew anims): frameAtlasAnim[anim][layer@base]; bases[b]: headOffset gets the six new anims, parts = union (+ top_gb_jacket, det_gb_vest), other keys are shallow-merged by anim name: boxPoint (+ carry_parcel, ring_doorbell, scan, tape_box; cityfolk's carry_box stays), handPoint (+ hand_parcel, sort_parcel - anim-keyed; officefolk's dir-keyed hand_over rows stay, no key collides), groundSpeed (+ carry_parcel), bellPoint, beamPoint, tapePoint, gbCover; tintTable[slot] union; generator.presets add (7 gb_* presets); palettes add (gb_*); other top-level keys (animItems, animFallback, geumbangfolkAnims, gbParts, gbPages, headPoseFallback, hub, brand ...) copied / shallow-merged.","Post rule (headPoseFallback): when the merged block has no head pose \"down\" (townfolk2 not merged), every geumbangfolk timeline frame with hp \"down\" uses \"nod\" instead (faces on those frames: neutral / blink / smile, which exist on \"nod\" too).  officefolk applies the same rule to its own anims.","canPlay(person, anim) = the officefolk / cityfolk rule plus: geumbangfolk anims need every worn body part (anim items excepted) in bases[b].gbCover[anim] (parts with an \"anims\" list: beachfolk_compose.partPlays); the new parts top_gb_jacket / det_gb_vest list exactly the anims they have frames in (6 crew anims + idle / walk / talk / wave / happy), so in every other anim (sit, run, desk_write ...) their wearer falls back.  pickAnim walks animFallback (carry_parcel -> walk + the game head-carries gb_parcel_*; ring_doorbell / hand_parcel -> talk -> idle; scan / sort_parcel / tape_box -> idle).","Acting anims (all but carry_parcel): arms, mittens, cuffs and items are drawn ABOVE the garments and the head stack in the front views (timeline zfront lists all four limbs in S / SE / E) - their frames are already cut wherever the body or the head hides them.  Nothing to do in the game: zfront is the townfolk rule.","Pages (gbPages): every geumbangfolk atlas is one page.  \"road\" (gbPages.resident) holds the courier anims, the cap (head frames) and the jacket / vest in the v4 anims: keep it resident wherever a 금방 courier or crew member is drawn.  \"hub\" (scan / sort_parcel / tape_box) is loaded while the depot is revealed.  pageNeeded(person, anim) is per person (the page holding the frames THAT person draws; the non-resident one when two are needed).","Game runtime (src/core/Townfolk.js TF, DollSprite): after TF.init(...) (+ TF.mergeOfficefolk when the office exists) merge the block and call geumbangfolk_compose.installGeumbangfolkRuntime(TF) once (recipe in docs/build_reports/gb_people.md).  It installs the officefolk draw-list runtime (layersIntoOF: frameAtlasAnim, animItems, onlyAnims / anims lists, zfrontFollow - generic, it draws the crew anims too) and sets TF.gb (and TF.of when officefolk is merged) to a Geumbangfolk instance: pickAnim, pageNeeded, parcelPoint, handPointOf, bellPoint, beamPoint, tapePoint, groundSpeed."],"notes":"Partial townfolk block (CONTRACT_GEUMBANG AP): the 금방 crew.  Merge after townfolk (+ townfolk2 / beachfolk / cityfolk / officefolk when present) with tools/geumbangfolk_compose.js mergeGeumbangfolk() (rules in \"merge\"), then compose exactly like tools/geumbangfolk_compose.py."}}